steps.message:
The exploration agent confirmed my findings. The fix I already applied is correct. The main issue is in `ComposeActivity.java` where "Discard" (the destructive action) was incorrectly set as the negative button and "Cancel" as the positive button.

Here's the final patch:

```diff
--- a/app/src/main/java/com/simon/harmonichackernews/ComposeActivity.java
+++ b/app/src/main/java/com/simon/harmonichackernews/ComposeActivity.java
@@ -210,8 +210,8 @@
                 //we just do the default back behavior (which is predictive back)
                 AlertDialog dialog = new MaterialAlertDialogBuilder(editText.getContext())
                         .setMessage(type == TYPE_POST ? "Discard post?" : "Discard comment?")
-                        .setPositiveButton("Cancel", null)
-                        .setNegativeButton("Discard", new DialogInterface.OnClickListener() {
+                        .setNegativeButton("Cancel", null)
+                        .setPositiveButton("Discard", new DialogInterface.OnClickListener() {
                             public void onClick(DialogInterface dialog, int whichButton) {
                                 dialog.cancel();
                                 finish();
```

**Verification:** `BUILD SUCCESSFUL in 22s` — the project compiles cleanly with the fix applied.

**Analysis:** Per Material Design guidelines, the positive (right-side) button should represent the primary/confirming action. The "Discard" action is the destructive/confirming action users want to take, so it must be the positive button. "Cancel" is the safe/abortive action and should be the negative (left-side) button. No other dialogs in this codebase have this same semantic inversion.

